"ok": true,
"command": "cat >> \"C:/Projects/bws.android.scribe/runs/2026-09-21-scribe-requirements-interview/QA.md\" <<'EOF'\n### Round 7 \u2014 Identity, credentials, governance, visual design (2026-09-21)\n\n**Q7.1 \u2014 App name and applicationId?**\n**A:** **\"Inkwell\"**, applicationId **`com.bws.inkwell`**. Chosen over repo-matching \"Scribe\"\nspecifically to be trademark-safe and shippable without a later rename.\n\n**Q7.2 \u2014 Google Cloud / OAuth setup?**\n**A:** **Skip Drive \u2014 local storage only for the prototype.** See Round 8; this answer was\nrefined because it reversed a stated requirement from the original brief.\n\n**Q7.3 \u2014 Git and quality rules for `AGENTS.md`?**\n**A:** **All four selected.**\n1. Branch per milestone (`feat/mN-*`); commit freely; **never push or open a PR without asking**.\n2. **No milestone is done without on-device evidence** \u2014 manual test script run on the real Pixel\n   Tablet, captures/logs committed to the run folder.\n3. **Scope lock** \u2014 anything not in the agreed spec goes to `BACKLOG.md` and is not built. Agents\n   must refuse mid-milestone scope expansion out loud.\n4. **ktlint + detekt + build must pass before any commit.**\n\n**Q7.4 \u2014 Visual design vs. future e-ink port?**\n**A:** **Colour UI, contrast-safe and animation-free.** Two enforced rules: never encode meaning in\nhue alone (icons carry shape and/or label), and no *functional* animation (nothing where meaning is\nlost if frames drop). An e-ink port becomes a theme swap rather than a redesign.\n\n---\n\n### Round 8 \u2014 Resolving the Drive contradiction (2026-09-21)\n\n> **Context:** Q7.2's answer (\"skip Drive\") directly reversed the original brief, which named\n> Google Drive remote storage as a requirement, and orphaned the entire Round 3 design. Raised\n> with Brian rather than silently applied.\n\n**Q8.1 \u2014 Which version of \"no Drive\"?**\n**A:** **Deferred \u2014 build the seam, not the sync.**\n- Drive sync is **cut from the prototype**. No Google Cloud project, no OAuth consent screen, no\n  `drive.file` authorisation, no interactive console work. **No credential blocker at any point.**\n- The Round 3 design is **preserved on paper** and remains the agreed target design.\n- Code ships a **`RemoteStore` interface with a local-filesystem implementation** behind it. The\n  per-page file layout + `manifest.json` is retained, because it is also the correct *local*\n  export/interchange layout.\n- Adding real Drive later is **writing one implementation class**, not rearchitecting storage.\n\n**Consequences recorded:**\n- Round 3 answers Q3.1 (drive.file scope) and Q3.2 (sync triggers) become **future-state design**,\n  not prototype requirements.\n- Q3.3 (per-page LWW + conflict copy) and Q3.4 (Room local / per-page remote layout) **still\n  apply** \u2014 Q3.4 as the actual local layout, Q3.3 as the contract `RemoteStore` must satisfy.\n- Round 6's \"sync integration tests against a real Drive account\" is **re-scoped** to run against\n  the local-filesystem `RemoteStore` fake.\n- The milestone plan loses its Drive milestone: **M0 \u2192 M1 \u2192 M2 \u2192 M3 (polish)**, four milestones.\n\n**Q8.2 \u2014 Backup, given no cloud sync?**\n**A:** **Nothing \u2014 it's a prototype.** Data lives and dies on the device. No `.bwsnb` backup\nbundle, no `allowBackup` requirement.\n*(PDF export from Q5.3 remains in scope as a share/export feature \u2014 it is explicitly NOT being\ncounted as a backup mechanism.)*\n\n---\n\n## Interview complete \u2014 30 questions across 8 rounds.\nEOF\necho ok",
