"command": "python - <<'EOF'\np='docs/design/specs/SPEC-THREAT.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold1=\"the stray spawned at `Spawn.Stray`, Anselm placed 5.8 m from it (the nearest member; Alrec and Moca are \u2265 23 m away)\"\nnew1=\"Anselm ordered to Stay (D-pad \u2190 tap) and placed 5.8 m from `Spawn.Stray`, then the stray spawned there (Anselm is the nearest member; Alrec and Moca are \u2265 23 m away)\"\nold2=\"**T03 script tuning this implies** (placement and waits only; the B1 asserts are unchanged): the good script waits for the stray's `HitWindup` on Anselm before the lock-on and taunt; it faces the stray itself (the driver's `Face` takes a marker, and the stray has left `Spawn.Stray` by then), or relies on the \u00a78 soft target; it ends 1 s after the first `HitLanded` on Alrec instead of a fixed 3 s, because P1 measures a cue's dwell to the session end when no `CueHidden` follows it.\"\nnew2=(\"**T03 script tuning this implies** (placement and waits only, through the driver's existing public steps; the B1 asserts are unchanged):\\n\"\n\"- **Pin Anselm with Stay** (`TapKey(Gamepad_DPad_Left)`, as SPEC-COMPANION-AI AT2) before placing him. Without it, U2's follow pulls him back to his slot behind Alrec, the stray follows him past Alrec, and it ends up behind Alrec's camera: `Face(Spawn.Stray)` (the driver's `Face` takes a marker only), the lock-on cone and the \u00a78 soft-target cone would all miss it. Pinned, the stray stays by `Spawn.Stray`, its wind-ups on Anselm repeat until the taunt (no HP in U3, so they cost nothing), and Stay exempts Anselm from the stuck oracle and the stranded fallback. The neglect run gets the same pin.\\n\"\n\"- The good script waits for the stray's `HitWindup` on Anselm before the lock-on and taunt (capture `stray-windup`).\\n\"\n\"- **The good run now requires a hit on Alrec:** it ends 1 s after the stray's first `HitLanded` on Alrec (a wait with a timeout, which fails the run if the hit never comes) instead of a fixed 3 s, because P1 measures a cue's dwell to the session end when no `CueHidden` follows it.\")\nassert old1 in s and old2 in s\ns=s.replace(old1,new1).replace(old2,new2)\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nh='runs/2026-09-26-m1-u3-taunt/HANDOFF.md'\nt=open(h,encoding='utf-8').read()\no=\"- `FTmsScenarioDriver::Face` takes a marker tag only. The stray has left `Spawn.Stray` when Alrec taunts; T03 must face the actor (script tuning) or rely on the \u00a78 soft target.\"\nn=\"- `FTmsScenarioDriver::Face` takes a marker tag only, and the soft target uses the same camera cone as lock-on. So B1's scripts must **pin Anselm with Stay** (`TapKey(Gamepad_DPad_Left)`, public on the driver) before placing him; otherwise follow drags him and the stray behind Alrec's camera. SPEC-THREAT \u00a711 T03 note.\"\no2=\"- U2 follow pulls Anselm back toward Alrec after `Place` (up to ~607 cm/s); perception runs every 0.1 s with a 12 m aggro radius, so the stray acquires him before he leaves.\"\nn2=\"- The good run now requires a `HitLanded` on Alrec (it ends 1 s after it), so every cue's dwell is measured.\"\nassert o in t and o2 in t\nt=t.replace(o,n).replace(o2,n2)\nopen(h,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(t)\nEOF\ngit add docs/design/specs/SPEC-THREAT.md && git commit -q -m \"SPEC-THREAT rev 1 draft: B1 scripts pin Anselm with Stay; good run requires a hit on Alrec (CMB-05, PRD-03; U3 N1)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -1 && git status --short && echo \"- Session 1 addendum: SPEC-THREAT AT1/T03 note revised (Stay pin for Anselm, good run requires a HitLanded on Alrec) after tracing the follow + camera-cone interaction; committed.\" >> runs/2026-09-26-m1-u3-taunt/RUNLOG.md",
