"ok": true,
"command": "cd /c/Users/bsmi0/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--Projects-tmsUnreal/3d4fa78d-9d4f-40b4-90ef-c12ac83c27ad/scratchpad\ncat > phase3-acceptance-criteria.md <<'EOF'\n# Phase 3 acceptance criteria \u2014 written BEFORE the evidence exists\nnpc-secondary, 2026-09-07. Same pre-flight pattern that worked on author_npc_binding.py and\nthe import path: state what would count, so the work is built to it rather than rejected after.\nHandoff line 225 (profiling) and line 206 (AC-08) are the source; nothing here is invented.\n\n## AC-08 \u2014 \"Real two-way rigged NPC/Alrec combat\"\nHandoff line 206: \"Real two-way rigged NPC/Alrec combat and correct disappearance/death/\naffiliation/unload invalidation\". Three load-bearing words:\n  REAL      -> gameplay, not an asset view. The handoff already records that a THUMBNAIL is\n               asset proof and not gameplay proof. The two PNGs on disk today are an Alrec\n               screenshot and a bear material thumbnail; neither is AC-08 evidence.\n  TWO-WAY   -> the NPC lands a hit on Alrec AND Alrec lands a hit on the NPC, in the same\n               encounter. A one-way capture is half the criterion.\n  RIGGED    -> the imported skeletal mesh and authored montage are what is on screen. A\n               capsule or a T-pose sliding on the spot is not \"rigged combat\" even if the\n               damage numbers are right.\nA08-1 Coverage named by the handoff: hostile melee, hostile ranged, wildlife, companion,\n      civilian. Five captures, not one. Ranged requires the archer, so it is gated on the\n      projectile path (register finding AC-21/22), not merely on the archer binding existing.\nA08-2 Each capture must be identifiable: which binding, which action, which map, when.\n      A capture that cannot be tied to a binding cannot discharge that binding.\nA08-3 The damage must be OBSERVABLE in the artifact, not asserted in prose beside it.\n      Health/state change visible, or a synchronized log excerpt from the same run.\nA08-4 NOT ACCEPTABLE, stated in advance so it is not argued later: a thumbnail; an editor\n      viewport with no play session; a montage previewed in the animation editor; a test log\n      with no visual; a capture of the acceptance grid with nothing fighting.\n\n## Population profiling \u2014 handoff line 225\nRequires: 25 / 50 / 100 active NPCs, mixed idle-sensing AND combat-heavy, recording hardware,\ncomposition, AI/perception/query CPU cost, pending work, and action/target-response latency.\nHardware is already named: i9-13980HX, ~64 GB, RTX 4070 Laptop.\nBudgets are DELIBERATELY UNSPECIFIED -- \"characterize honestly and keep that product\nprerequisite explicit\". So this cannot fail for being slow. It can only fail for being untrue.\nThat inverts where the scrutiny goes: not at the numbers, at whether they measure anything.\n\nP-1 ANTI-THROTTLE PROOF. The handoff explicitly disqualifies the earlier ~3 FPS\n    background-throttled PIE. So the run must carry positive evidence it was not throttled:\n    editor \"Use Less CPU when in Background\" disabled, or a standalone/-game run rather than\n    a backgrounded PIE, plus a frame-time series consistent with a foreground run. State\n    which. A number without this is inadmissible no matter how good it looks.\nP-2 THE VACUITY CONTROL, and the one I care most about. 100 NPCs that are dormant, asleep,\n    or aware of nothing cost almost nothing and would profile beautifully while proving\n    nothing. The run must show the NPCs are DOING the work being measured: non-zero\n    perception updates, targets actually acquired, queries actually run. Without this,\n    \"100 NPCs at high FPS\" is the profiling form of a check that passes without verifying.\n    npc-main's dormancy flag makes this a real risk -- a placed-but-dormant source is exactly\n    the thing that would inflate the count without the cost.\nP-3 SCALING MUST BE VISIBLE. The same scenario at three sizes. Cost should rise with N; if\n    25/50/100 are flat, that is evidence the population is not actually active (see P-2),\n    not evidence of excellent scaling. Flatness is a RED FLAG, not a result.\nP-4 COMPOSITION STATED. 100 hares is not 100 NPCs for AI cost. Record the binding mix per\n    run; hostile/companion/civilian differ in perception range, action count and party work.\nP-5 BOTH SCENARIOS. Mixed idle/sensing AND combat-heavy are separate rows, not one blended\n    average. They stress different systems and the handoff names both.\nP-6 LATENCY IS ACTION/TARGET RESPONSE, not frame time. Frame time is the cheap number and it\n    is not what line 225 asks for. Needs the time from stimulus to target acquisition and\n    from request to action start.\nP-7 HONEST CHARACTERIZATION INCLUDES THE BAD ROW. If 100 is unplayable on this hardware, that\n    is a valid and complete result, and the handoff explicitly says to keep the prerequisite\n    explicit rather than to hit a number. Do not tune the scenario until it passes; there is\n    nothing to pass.\n\n## StateTree post-restart round-trip (TASKLIST 33)\nThe regen receipt's reload runs in the SAME session, so it proves residency, not round-trip.\nNeeds the verify step after an actual Editor restart, as wolf's D8 did.\nEOF\necho written; wc -l phase3-acceptance-criteria.md",
