"command": "python - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/design/specs/SPEC-THREAT.md'); s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old[:60]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"now waits on a group-coordination spec.\", \"now waits on a group-coordination spec. **Revision 2 edits (U5b, SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a717.1)**, 2026-09-26: the target resolver, the pressure ledger, committed actions and schema v2 refs.\")\nrep(\"The chosen member's entry becomes `AcquireThreat` (if lower).\", \"The chosen member's entry becomes `AcquireThreat` (if lower). A participant of a **Dormant** encounter does not acquire until its encounter is Alerted (SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a710: Alrec seen, player hostility, reveal or alarm); ungrouped enemies are unchanged.\")\nrep(\"2. **Current target.** Without a force (rule 5), the current target is kept\", \"2. **Threat target** (tier 8 of SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a77). The enemy's resolved victim comes from the target resolver; without a higher tier it is the threat target. Without a force (rule 5), the threat target is kept\")\nrep(\"Only Alrec forces in M1.\", \"Only Alrec forces in M1. A force is tier 3: it defeats tiers 4\u20138 on `Forced` archetypes but not an attached hold (tier 2).\")\nrep(\"The Thrall is Forced.\\n\", \"The Thrall is Forced. `BiasMode = Multiplier` scales the matching members' values inside the switch rule only; both margins apply to the scaled values (SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a77.2).\\n\")\nrep(\"8. **Target changes** write `ThreatChanged`\", \"8. **Resolved-victim changes** (any tier), each starting a new target epoch whose ref `ThreatChanged` carries, write `ThreatChanged`\")\nold9 = s[s.index(\"9. **Retarget tell**\"):s.index(\"## 3. Threat event table\")]\ns = s.replace(old9, \"9. **Retarget tell** (PRE-02: \\\"retargets get a 0.5 s tell\\\"). After any resolved-victim change the enemy turns to face its new victim and does not start a wind-up for `RetargetTellSeconds`. An **uncommitted** action on the old victim (Startup; the Thrall's wind-up) is cancelled at once (CMB-03: \\\"Taunt changes intent\\\") and its reservation released. A **committed** action (Active, Recovery; SPEC-MOVESETS \u00a78 rule 2) finishes against its original victim; the change applies to the next action. A released projectile or live hazard is never recalled and keeps its reservation (SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a77 rule 4, \u00a79.3).\\n\\n\")\nold4 = s[s.index(\"## 4. Melee attack tokens\"):s.index(\"## 5. Combat state\")]\ns = s.replace(old4, \"## 4. Melee attack tokens (CMB-04; SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a79)\\n- Melee attack tokens are the `Melee` dimension of the shared pressure ledger (SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a79); the same per-victim numbers (Alrec 3, Moca 2, Anselm 1) live in `DA_GroupConfig`. An enemy requests admission before its wind-up and releases per the slot's lifetime. An enemy in reach that is refused **waits** at `WaitRingCm`, facing its victim, and asks again each tick. `UTmsThreatConfig::Tokens` is removed.\\n\\n\")\nrep(\"- The world is **in combat** while any enemy has a current target or any threat entry.\", \"- The world is **in combat** while any enemy has a resolved victim or any threat entry, or the pressure ledger holds any hostile reservation, or an engaged encounter has an unresolved required arrival (SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a79.5).\")\nold6 = s[s.index(\"## 6. Valid targets and invalid-target removal\"):s.index(\"## 7. The Skeleton Thrall\")]\ns = s.replace(old6, \"## 6. Valid targets and invalid-target removal\\n- A party member is a valid target unless tier 1 of SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a77 excludes it (Downed, Captured, removed, encounter-protected, reserved by another holder's Condemned hold); rows wired by U8 (Downed) and M2 (holds). In U5b every party member is valid except in synthetic tests.\\n- When a member becomes invalid, its entry is removed from every table; every uncommitted action on it is cancelled (`Invalidated`) and its reservation released; committed and in-flight actions on it resolve no contact at impact, and live projectiles and hazards keep their reservations until they resolve (SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a77 rule 5, \u00a79.4). Each enemy that targeted it resolves again. A force whose target (Alrec) becomes invalid ends without its end-of-force rule.\\n- When an enemy is removed (destroyed, or the fixture's `Reset`), its `ActionEnd` reservations are released and its glyph and melee ring end (`Removed`); its released projectiles and hazards keep theirs (SPEC-UI-HUD \u00a74).\\n\\n\")\nrep(\"| Idle | Stands at its post; perceives (\u00a72 rule 1) | It has a target \u2192 Tell |\", \"| Idle | Stands at its post; perceives (\u00a72 rule 1) | It has a resolved victim \u2192 Tell |\")\nrep(\"| Tell | Turns toward the new target, `RetargetTellSeconds` | Time up \u2192 Chase |\", \"| Tell | Turns toward the new victim, `RetargetTellSeconds` | Time up \u2192 Chase |\")\nrep(\"| Chase | Paths to its target at `ChaseSpeed`; re-paths every `RepathSeconds` (0.25 s) | Within `AttackStartCm` \u2192 WaitToken |\", \"| Chase | Paths to its victim at `ChaseSpeed`; re-paths every `RepathSeconds` (0.25 s) | Within `AttackStartCm` \u2192 WaitAdmission |\")\nrep(\"| WaitToken | Holds at `WaitRingCm`, faces the target (\u00a74) | Token taken \u2192 WindUp; target out of `AttackStartCm` + 50 \u2192 Chase |\", \"| WaitAdmission | Holds at `WaitRingCm`, faces the victim, requests admission each tick (\u00a74) | Admitted and revalidated on the next tick (SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a79.2 rule 4) \u2192 WindUp; victim out of `AttackStartCm` + 50 \u2192 Chase |\")\nrep(\"| WindUp | Writes `HitWindup`; stands, turns toward the target at `WindupTurnRate` | `WindupSeconds` \u2192 Strike; cancelled by a target change \u2192 Tell |\", \"| WindUp | Writes `HitWindup`; stands, turns toward the victim at `WindupTurnRate` (uncommitted) | `WindupSeconds` \u2192 Strike; cancelled by a resolved-victim change \u2192 Tell |\")\nrep(\"| Strike | One frame: the hit lands if the target's centre is within `ReachCm` (2D) and inside \u00b1`ArcDegrees` of the Thrall's facing | \u2192 Recover |\", \"| Strike | One frame (committed): the hit lands if the victim's centre is within `ReachCm` (2D) and inside \u00b1`ArcDegrees` of the Thrall's facing and the victim is still eligible; a resolved-victim change does not affect it | \u2192 Recover |\")\nrep(\"| Recover | Stands `RecoverSeconds`, then releases the token | \u2192 Chase |\", \"| Recover | Stands `RecoverSeconds` (committed; a resolved-victim change does not affect it), then releases the reservation | \u2192 Chase, or Tell if the victim changed meanwhile |\")\nrep(\"Any target change moves the Thrall to Tell (\u00a72 rule 9).\", \"A resolved-victim change moves the Thrall to Tell, except in Strike and Recover, where the action finishes first (\u00a72 rule 9).\")\nrep(\"- Events written in U3:\", \"- Since U5b, events carry refs (SPEC-ACCEPT schema v2; SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a711). Events written in U3:\")\nrep(\"| AT3 | **Tokens**, `TMS.Fast.Threat.Tokens` (fast tier) | The pure token pool | Anselm grants 1, Moca 2, Alrec 3; a fourth taker on Alrec waits; release on recovery end, cancel and removal frees the token | Exact | Fast-tier report |\",\n    \"| AT3 | **Melee dimension**, `TMS.Fast.Threat.Tokens` (fast tier) | The pure pressure ledger (SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS \u00a79) | The ledger's melee dimension grants Anselm 1, Moca 2, Alrec 3; a fourth on Alrec waits; release on recovery end, cancel and removal | Exact | Fast-tier report |\")\nrep(\"| `Tokens` Alrec / Moca / Anselm | 3 / 2 / 1 (CMB-04) |\\n\", \"\")\nrep(\"- **C++ state machine, not a StateTree (TEC-03 recommends StateTree),**\", \"- **Group coordination (rev 2):** the precondition below is met by SPEC-ENEMY-GROUPS; architecture per its \u00a72 (C++ kernel; the Thrall stays a C++ state machine; StateTree only as an executor later).\\n- **C++ state machine, not a StateTree (TEC-03 recommends StateTree),**\")\np.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8'); print(\"ok\")\nEOF\ngrep -n \"token\" docs/design/specs/SPEC-THREAT.md",
